{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","externalID":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":") for a Google Analytics 4 stream in one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call. It checks the measurement ID and the API secret, and posts to the Measurement Protocol’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/mp\/collect"},{"type":"text","text":" endpoint of the region ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion"},{"type":"text","text":") with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":". It splits each batch to the Measurement Protocol’s limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"type":"text","text":"): 25 events and 100 KB a request. A batch with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"The-API-secret-stays-on-a-server","level":3,"text":"The API secret stays on a server"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol takes only requests that carry one of the stream’s API secrets, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anyone holding that secret can send events to the property. Google’s docs say not to expose it in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an app, and an app’s binary can be read by anyone who installs it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So the whole module is compiled for macOS and Linux alone, where a server runs. An app for iOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iPadOS, tvOS, watchOS, visionOS or Mac Catalyst that calls the factory, or names the encoder, fails","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to compile. A Mac app, AppKit or SwiftUI, compiles the factory as a Mac server does, but the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factory refuses it at run time: it throws ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError\/appBundle","isActive":true},{"text":" when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"process’s main bundle is an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".app"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".appex"},{"text":". Nothing stops a Mac app from building an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" with this encoder and an endpoint it writes itself, secret and all, so don’t.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The secret is also in the query of every request’s URL. Don’t log the destination, its requests or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a transport’s URLs."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError","type":"reference"},{"text":" for an empty measurement ID, for one that isn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"G-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" followed by uppercase letters and digits, and for an empty API secret. The region has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default: ","type":"text"},{"code":".global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is Google’s default endpoint, and ","type":"text"},{"code":".eu","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has Google collect the data in the EU.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Getting-an-apps-events-to-Google-Analytics","level":3,"text":"Getting an app’s events to Google Analytics"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An app’s events reach Google Analytics through a server of yours: the app sends them there, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the server makes this destination and hands it the records. Traffluent doesn’t provide that server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yet. TraffluentCollector receives an app’s batches, but it doesn’t forward them to Google","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Analytics, and Traffluent has no decoder that turns a collector batch back into records.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Until it does, the server’s job is:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read each event the app sent (its name, version, identifier, timestamp, properties and session)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and decode it into the same ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type the app tracked, from a module the app and the server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Remake its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord(id:event:timestamp:sourceLocation:context:)"},{"text":": the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"app’s identifier and timestamp, and a context whose ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":" is the app’s session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand each batch of records to the destination’s "},{"code":"receive(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t track the events again through a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":".sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on the server. That tracker","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would give every event the server’s own session, so every user of the app would arrive in Google","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Analytics as one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A server that tracks its own events, rather than an app’s, uses a tracker as any app does:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let googleAnalytics = try HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(","    measurementID: measurementID,  \/\/ the web or data stream's, G-…","    apiSecret: apiSecret,  \/\/ from the server's configuration, never an app's","    region: .global,  \/\/ or .eu, to have Google collect the data in the EU","    plan: plan)","\/\/ A server tracking its own events: its sessions are the server's.","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: googleAnalytics)"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-Google-Analytics-receives","level":3,"text":"What Google Analytics receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request holds one client’s events, as the Measurement Protocol takes one ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, written as the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"halves of its UUID in decimal, joined by a period, the form the Measurement Protocol asks for. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record with no session is sent under its own record identifier, in a request of its own. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter is the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, so Google Analytics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"groups the session’s events, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp_micros","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s timestamp. Every request","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sends ad consent as denied, so Google uses none of the events for advertising.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", user properties, location, IP address, device or user agent is sent, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"advertising identifier. The record’s vendor identifier, trace context and standard context aren’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent either. Google Analytics counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports, and so is each record sent without a session.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"engagement_time_msec","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent, as Traffluent doesn’t measure engagement. Without it the events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"don’t count toward engagement time or engaged sessions, and the Realtime and Users reports can show","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no users while events arrive. Check the event counts, not the user counts, to see that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination works.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and become the event’s "},{"code":"params","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Google Analytics takes only strings, numbers and booleans, so a nested value is spread into a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"parameter for each value it holds, named after its path joined by "},{"code":"_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"cart_size","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tags_0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Records-sent-twice","level":3,"text":"Records sent twice"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol has no field that identifies an event, so Google Analytics can’t tell a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"repeat from a new event, and counts every one it receives. A record is sent more than once when a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request is retried after Google stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cancelled batch again, and when a store redelivers records after a relaunch. Each such record is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counted twice in Google Analytics."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Records-left-out","level":3,"text":"Records left out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name, or a parameter’s name, is longer than 40 bytes, doesn’t start with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letter, or holds anything but letters, numbers and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":";"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name Google Analytics keeps ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_start"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"first_visit"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of its reserved names), or takes only from an app stream ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_view"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ad_impression"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in_app_purchase"},{"type":"text","text":");"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a parameter Google Analytics keeps (a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"firebase_"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ga_"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"google_"},{"type":"text","text":" prefix) or named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", which the encoder writes;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one of more than 25 parameters, counting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"},{"type":"text","text":", or with a string longer than 100 bytes;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one tracked more than 72 hours before the batch is encoded, or more than 15 minutes after it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one whose timestamp has no microseconds form;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one too large for a request.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Google Analytics wouldn’t refuse such an event: it answers 2xx either way. Under its default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relaxed validation it stores the event without the parameter that breaks a rule, or under a name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it never checked, so the report would hold an event other than the one tracked. The encoder leaves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the record out and reports it instead. A Google Analytics 360 property takes values of up to 500","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters, but the encoder holds every property to the standard 100 bytes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The destination reports each as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" whose reason is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"},{"text":". The encoder logs a notice for each event and property of the plan","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named as Google Analytics refuses when the destination is made; rename such an event or property,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"raising the event’s version, to send it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"What-the-Measurement-Protocol-doesnt-report","level":3,"text":"What the Measurement Protocol doesn’t report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol answers 2xx to every request it receives, including one it can’t read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose events it doesn’t store. A wrong measurement ID or API secret is answered 2xx with nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored, so check the property’s Realtime event counts after setting the destination up. Google’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"validation server, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/debug\/mp\/collect"},{"type":"text","text":", checks a body’s shape but not the measurement ID or the API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"secret, so a body it accepts can still be stored nowhere. A record older than 72 hours is stored as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if it happened 72 hours ago, so the encoder leaves those out too; a request retried for long after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its batch was encoded can still arrive past that window."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to PostHog, Amplitude, Mixpanel or Segment, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AmplitudeEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MixpanelEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SegmentSpecEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Google Analytics receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Google-Analytics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsRegion","doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Google Analytics"},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches"},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out"}],"references":{"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records from a server to a Google Analytics 4 web or data stream through the Measurement Protocol."}],"title":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder\/batchlimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","title":"batchLimit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Measurement Protocol’s limits on one request: 25 events and 100,000 bytes of body, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s included."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","title":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference"},{"text":" of Google Analytics 4’s Measurement Protocol, so an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" on a server can send events to a web or data stream’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/mp\/collect"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/googleanalyticsencoding\/googleanalyticsbatchencoder","type":"topic"},"doc://GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/documentation/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/documentation\/GoogleAnalyticsEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination on a server that sends batches to the Google Analytics web or data stream of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"measurementID"},{"type":"text","text":", authenticated by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"apiSecret"},{"type":"text","text":", with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession.shared"},{"type":"text","text":", retrying a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send that fails for now with the waits of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transport"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSessionTransport"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encoding"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GoogleAnalyticsBatchEncoder"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]},"title":"googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"googleAnalytics","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"measurementID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"apiSecret","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"region","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:23GoogleAnalyticsEncoding0aB6RegionO","text":"GoogleAnalyticsRegion","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"plan","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"E